namespace com.linkedin.metadata.query

/**
 * Whether to check that schema fields read off the lineage graph still exist, by reading the
 * schemaMetadata of the datasets holding them. The graph keeps its edges long after a column is
 * removed from a schema or its dataset is deleted, so results read off it include columns that are
 * no longer there.
 */
enum SchemaFieldValidationMode {

  /**
   * Do not check. Results may include columns their parent no longer declares.
   */
  NONE

  /**
   * Check when it is cheap to, which is nearly always: the read is batched per parent dataset and
   * columns share parents heavily, so a walk over very many columns is usually few reads. Skipped
   * when a walk fans out over more parent datasets than are worth fetching.
   */
  AUTO

  /**
   * Check however many parent datasets it takes.
   */
  ALWAYS
}
